{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "292061208",
    "title": "TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292061208",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 8,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "1-overview1. Overview\n---------------------\n\nProduct data in the Zimmermann SFCC platform is managed through a **master catalogue** (`zimmermann-catalog`) with per-site **storefront catalogues** for navigation and category assignment. Product content (rich text, editorial imagery) is managed in **Contentful CMS**.\n\nAP21 is the system of record for all product data. Product data flows from AP21 into SFCC via **MuleSoft** — there is no direct AP21 → SFCC integration. MuleSoft acts as the integration layer, transforming and routing product data into SFCC catalogue XML imports.\n\n---\n\n2-product-data-architecture2. Product Data Architecture\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nDefaultnoneAP21 (ERP — system of record for products)\n│\n└──► MuleSoft (integration layer — transform + route)\n│\n└──► zimmermann-catalog (SFCC master catalogue)\n│ products + variants + attributes\n│\n├──► zimmermann-au-storefront-catalog (AU nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-uk-storefront-catalog (UK nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-us-storefront-catalog (US domestic nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-us-intl-storefront-catalog (US International / Global-e nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-eu-storefront-catalog (EU nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-eu-intl-storefront-catalog (EU International / Global-e nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-hk-storefront-catalog (HK nav categories)\n└──► zimmermann-me-storefront-catalog (ME nav categories)\nContentful CMS\n│\n└──► PWA Kit (editorial content: banners, editorial copy, lookbook)\nvia Contentful Delivery API\n\n---\n\n3-master-catalogue-structure3. Master Catalogue Structure\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Catalogue ID:**`zimmermann-catalog`\n\n### 31-category-hierarchy-all-storefront-catalogues3.1 Category Hierarchy (all storefront catalogues)\n\n| Position | Category ID | Display Name | Sub-categories |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `new-arrivals` | New | — |\n| 2 | `clothing` | Clothing | dresses, tops, bottoms, knitwear, jackets, swimwear |\n| 3 | `accessories` | Accessories | bags, shoes, jewellery |\n| 4 | `collections` | Collections | resort |\n| 5 | `z-immerse` | Z.Immerse | — |\n| 6 | `sale` | Sale | — |\n\n**Magento-sourced category hierarchy** (used during Magento migration — see Section 11):\n\nDefaultnoneroot\n└── {prodline} (L1 — e.g. \"collection\")\n└── {prodline}-{prodsub} (L2 — product assignment target, e.g. \"collection-tops-blouse\")\n\n`categoryap21` is an internal AP21 ERP code — stored as a hidden custom attribute (`ap21Category`) on the product, not used for storefront navigation.\n\n### 32-product-model3.2 Product Model\n\nSFCC product types in use:\n\n| Type | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Master product | Top-level product identified by `stylecode` — holds variation attributes (colour, size), images, descriptions |\n| Variant product | Individual purchasable SKU — `stylecode` + `colourcode` + `sizecode` |\n| Color group (Magento) | Style + colour SKU in Magento (`visibility = Catalog, Search`) — maps to master product body |\n\n**Product ID conventions:**\n\n| SFCC Role | ID Pattern | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Master | `stylecode` | `4673TS251` |\n| Variant | `stylecode` + `colourcode` + `sizecode` | `4673TS251GVSCP0P` |\n\n---\n\n4-catalogue-import-process4. Catalogue Import Process\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\n### 41-initial-load-sample-data4.1 Initial Load (Sample Data)\n\nA filtered sample catalogue (`data/sample/catalogs/zimmermann-catalog/`) is used for development and staging bootstrapping.\n\n**Import command:**\n\nDefaultbashnpm run data:import:sample\n\n### 42-ongoing-product-feed4.2 Ongoing Product Feed\n\n| Step | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Source | AP21 (ERP) — system of record for all product master data |\n| Integration layer | MuleSoft — receives product events from AP21, transforms to SFCC Catalog XML, and delivers to SFCC |\n| Format | SFCC Catalog XML (catalog.xsd compliant) |\n| Target | `zimmermann-catalog` (master) + per-site storefront catalogues |\n| Trigger | MuleSoft event-driven (AP21 product create / update) or scheduled batch — to be confirmed with MuleSoft team |\n| Import method | MuleSoft → SFCC OCAPI Data API (`/s/-/dw/data/v*/catalogs`) or SFCC SFTP + import job |\n\n### 43-product-imagery4.3 Product Imagery\n\nProduct images are loaded directly into SFCC — there is no Cloudinary or external DAM involved. Images are stored in the SFCC static content library and referenced from product records by path.\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Storage | SFCC static content library (loaded directly) |\n| Source | AP21 / DAM — images are uploaded directly to SFCC; no Cloudinary or external DAM in the pipeline |\n| Image types | Large, medium, small/thumbnail, hi-res model shot, swatch/styling shot |\n| Migration reference | Magento image paths used as source reference during initial load only |\n\n---\n\n5-storefront-catalogue-assignment5. Storefront Catalogue Assignment\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEach site's storefront catalogue is set in `preferences.xml` via `SiteCatalog`:\n\n| Site | Storefront Catalogue |\n| --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `zimmermann-au-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannUK | `zimmermann-uk-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannUS | `zimmermann-us-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | `zimmermann-us-intl-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannEU | `zimmermann-eu-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | `zimmermann-eu-intl-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannHK | `zimmermann-hk-storefront-catalog` |\n| ZimmermannME | `zimmermann-me-storefront-catalog` |\n\nThe master catalogue assignment (linking storefront categories to master products) is managed in SFCC Business Manager — it cannot be set via XML import.\n\n---\n\n6-contentful-cms-integration6. Contentful CMS Integration\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Purpose | Editorial content: hero banners, collection pages, lookbook, rich PDP copy |\n| Rendering | PWA Kit fetches content at runtime via Contentful Delivery API |\n| Scope | Non-product content; all product data remains in SFCC catalogue sourced from AP21 via MuleSoft |\n\n---\n\n7-multilocale-product-content7. Multi-Locale Product Content\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Site | Locales | Language Tags |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | en | `x-default`, `en` |\n| ZimmermannUK | en, en\\_GB | `x-default`, `en`, `en-GB` |\n| ZimmermannUS | en, en\\_US | `x-default`, `en`, `en-US` |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | en, en\\_US | `x-default`, `en`, `en-US` |\n| ZimmermannEU | en, en\\_GB, fr, it, es | `x-default`, `en`, `fr`, `it`, `es` |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | en, en\\_CH | `x-default`, `en`, `en-CH` |\n| ZimmermannHK | en, en\\_HK | `x-default`, `en`, `en-HK` |\n| ZimmermannME | en, en\\_AE | `x-default`, `en`, `en-AE` |\n\nProduct XML attributes use `xml:lang` for each locale. The `x-default` value is always English.\n\n---\n\n8-product-display-page-pdp--mulesoft-touchpoints8. Product Display Page (PDP) — MuleSoft Touchpoints\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMuleSoft is the integration layer for the product import pipeline (see Section 4.2). In addition, the PDP has two further MuleSoft-dependent runtime features:\n\n| Feature | API | Detail |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Find In Store / Boutique Stock | `product-availibility-prc-api` | Real-time store stock availability shown on PDP |\n| Real-time DC stock check | [TBC] | Online availability from NewStore fulfilment groups |\n\n---\n\n9-key-design-decisions9. Key Design Decisions\n---------------------------------------------\n\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Product source of truth | AP21 | AP21 is the ERP and master for all product data |\n| Product integration layer | MuleSoft | Consistent with Zimmermann integration platform; MuleSoft handles AP21 event consumption, transformation, and SFCC delivery |\n| Product imagery | Loaded directly into SFCC | No external DAM or Cloudinary in the pipeline; images stored in SFCC static content library |\n| Catalogue structure | One master + eight storefront catalogues | SFCC best practice for multi-site |\n| Editorial content | Contentful | Decouples editorial from product data; supports headless PWA pattern |\n| Category positions | Explicit `<position>` elements per category | Ensures nav order matches Figma design across all sites |\n| USIntl separate storefront catalogue | `zimmermann-us-intl-storefront-catalog` | Allows independent category assignment for Global-e international customers |\n\n---\n\n10-open-items10. Open Items\n---------------------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm MuleSoft delivery mechanism to SFCC — OCAPI Data API vs SFTP + import job; confirm trigger (event-driven vs scheduled batch) | Integration Lead / MuleSoft team | Open |\n| 2 | Confirm product attribute set required for SFCC | Zimmermann Merch team | **Closed** — see [TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345) |\n| 3 | Define Contentful content model and connector customisation scope | Frontend Dev | Open |\n| 4 | Product imagery source and pipeline | Zimmermann Digital | **Closed** — images loaded directly into SFCC static content library; no Cloudinary or external DAM in pipeline |\n| 5 | Confirm whether ZimmermannUSIntl storefront catalogue requires different category structure or promotions vs ZimmermannUS | Zimmermann US Merch | Open |\n| 6 | Confirm Magento store\\_id → SFCC site mapping for stores 6, 9, 12, 18, 19, 22, 25, 28, 35, 38, 40, 43 | Integration Lead | Open |\n\n---\n\n11-product-attribute-mapping11. Product Attribute Mapping\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe full AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC product attribute mapping (system attributes, custom attributes, pricebook conventions, and ignored fields) has been extracted to a dedicated page:\n\n➡️ **[TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345)**\n\nThat page is derived from the Magento product CSV export (`sfccexport.csv`) and verified against the Magento staging REST API. The conversion script lives at `scripts/magento-to-sfcc.js` in the `zimmermann-sfccworkplace` repository.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

